sma-airs-desktop. Production config independently names Prisma AIRS Desktop1.0.0/io.cdot.airs-desktop. Native About/menu/title and Home-first catalogue agree; startup/settings/sessions focus and headings use the one presentation. Exact candidate process identity, executable and complete bundle are bound.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C45-N02\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"observation\": \"Fresh wizard and fresh relaunch expose no controlled prior canary, and controlled alpha/v2 canaries remain byte-identical across fixture cleanup/relaunch. Actual FileStore setup/restart/reset and four service isolation are separate required production-interface checks in qualification.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/planning/evidence/C45/baseline-03/identity/observations.json\",\n        \"docs/planning/evidence/C45/baseline-03/identity/fresh-relaunch.json\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Fresh synthetic setup starts with the wizard and no adopted tenants, credentials, sessions or approvals. Controlled prior alpha/v2 root/service canaries remain byte-identical across setup/relaunch/reset. Old real application roots, login Keychain and live endpoints are never inspected. Namespace isolation and non-adoption require passing production-interface FileStore/authority and disposable-file Keychain regressions, not only absence of UI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C45-N03\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"observation\": \"The current same-candidate mapped native suite and production-interface/frontend regressions are separately required by qualification for ordinary collections, active helpers, removed intents and all current native assertions. This row explicitly binds their required aggregate rather than claiming they ran within this driver.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/planning/evidence/C45/baseline-03/native-acceptance.json\",\n        \"docs/planning/evidence/C45/baseline-03/identity/observations.json\"\n      ],\n      \"descripti